{
  "id": "session-summaries1",
  "title": "Session Summaries",
  "thumbnail": "https://media.easy-peasy.ai/07f829c6-75b3-43c9-9dda-739fa514d25e/b335938f-b919-4709-a6dd-b11bef929645.png",
  "description": "",
  "content": "<div><br></div><div><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><h1><span style=\"font-size: 16pt; font-family: Montserrat, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\">Session 29 - “Egg-scape from Demogorgon” 3/27/26</font></span></h1><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.7999999999999998;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\">Played this session: Daterra, Perry, Sig, Jibjib, Kronk</font></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.7999999999999998;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\">Before session 30, level up to Level 8!</font></span></p><font color=\"#ffffff\"><ul><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><font color=\"#ffffff\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.6667px; white-space: pre;\"><br></span></font></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 700; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Next Time.&nbsp;</span></span></li></ul></font><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.7999999999999998;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\">Current Objectives:&nbsp;</font></span></p><ul><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Find your Stolen Things.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Find out who framed you for stealing things from Hourglass Coven hag sisters.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Find the missing unicorn horn to unfreeze Zybilna in her palace.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">End the Hags’ tyranny over Prismeer.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Solve Bavlorna's Big Book of Bad Blood.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Solve the Puzzle Box.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Rescue remaining kids from Loomlurch: Mishka, Sigh, Puddlemore, Squid, Elkhorn.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Stop the demons pouring into the Underdark from the Abyss.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Solve the Ollie copies plot. “Radnelac”, “Smite”, etc.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Bring Nib furnishings for his home.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Go to Gracklstugh (the capital city of the gray dwarves), Skab wants a captive dragon investigated and preferably freed from the dwarves.&nbsp;</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Go to Neverlight Grove (home of the myconids like Shrump), Skab wants Daterra to collect spores or mushrooms from the heart of the grove and bring back to her for her alchemical experiments.&nbsp;</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Go to Blingdenstone (Sig's hometown and capital city of the deep gnomes), Skab wants a so-called \"king\" there investigated in case he is a threat to Skab and others.</span></span></li></ul><font color=\"#ffffff\"><br></font><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.7999999999999998;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\">Mysteries &amp; Leads:&nbsp;</font></span></p><ul><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Rifts between Underdark, Feywild, and Abyss. “Faerzress” and “fairy circles” amplified.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Jibjib learned of conspiracies from his Patron. Also warned to return to Underdark asap.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Demons are pouring into the Underdark through portals for some reason.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;\">Zybilna and/or her Palace staff members have powerful magic items, make magic circles, and know about defeating/trapping demons.</span></span></li></ul><font color=\"#ffffff\"><br></font><h1><span style=\"font-size: 16pt; font-family: Montserrat, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\">Session 28 - “It Was a Trap!” 2/6/26</font></span></h1><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.7999999999999998;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;\"><font color=\"#ffffff\">Played this session: Daterra, Perry, Sig, Jibjib, Kronk</font></span></p><ul><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">Sig recognized where they were:</span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"> the Whorlstone Tunnels beneath the dwarven city Gracklstugh. Sig realized after Riftwalking here, it seemed to be a big coincidence that they happened to fall directly into a deadly pit of zombies.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">Runk the Derro.</span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"> After escaping the zombie pit, the Party had the little derro guy, named Runk, restrained. Runk was terrified and confused about Daterra's Demogorgon forehead scar, but he agreed to take them to his master, a derro named Narrak. But Runk refused to lead the way, scared of all the dangers in the tunnels.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">Yellow Mold. </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">The Party encountered Yellow Mold hazards that damaged Daterra. They were able to jump or toss everyone past.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">Traps.</span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"> Daterra fell into a pit trap in the ground. Then they found a Shrieker, a mushroom that screams in alarm when approached. Daterra was able to speak to the mushroom to silence it before it screamed.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">Approaching the Cult Ritual.</span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"> With Sig and Jib disguised as derros, and Kronk and Perry acting as Daterra's bodyguards, the Party convinced the derros that Daterra was a cult leader needing to talk to Narrak. This allowed them to get in close to a group of derros performing a demonic ritual in a huge magic circle. Perry then walked right up… and slapped Narrak in the face for not honoring “cult leader” Daterra!</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">Combat.</span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"> Narrak and his derro cultists attacked using demonic tentacles and psychic attacks. A two-headed giant, or “ettin”, also attacked, but the Party avoided having a Death Dog loosed from its cage. Jibjib kept a safe distance, using blasts, summons, and Hunger of Hadar within the entire magic circle. Sig gave massive healing. Perry tanked up close. Daterra summoned an elemental but was then KO'd. Kronk also got targeted a ton, getting frozen by Hold Person. But then in the end Kronk was unleashed and slaughtered enemies, including killing Narrak and Spartan-kicking him backward into Jibjib's Hadar tentacle darkness. Epic.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">The Ritual Magic Circle. </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">The magic circle used by Narrak and the derros had a couple statues in the center. The cultists were doing some ritual to curse certain stone giants in the city above by making them grow second heads and go Mad.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">Sig Madness. </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">After combat, Sig did some mysterious rituals for Mr. Sixx. Walking within the cultist magic circle gave Sig a Madness that made him forget the existence of everyone around. Exhausted and confused, Sig simply set up camp in the corner of the cavern. Unsure what else to do, the rest of the Party rested there too.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">Shuushar's Betrayal.</span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\"> During the night, Shuushar visited Kronk for one last \"Jedi training\" dream, telling him the tale of “the Tragedy of Belaphoss the Mad”, a lieutenant of Demogorgon. It was revealed that Shuushar had been fattening the Party up to sacrifice them to his master, Demogorgon! </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">HE </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">helped Jorlan the drow guard summon demons at Velkenvelve in the very beginning, helping the Party break out of prison... </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">HE </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">was the one that sacrificed his entire city of Sloobludop to Demogorgon when he summoned his master there... He was \"leveled up\" with better stats and granted the ability to speak Common by his master... He had been faking being a pacifish, being wise and enlightened and prophetic... </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">HE </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">was the one helping to divert Sig to Riftwalk right into a pit of zombies in the Whorlstone Tunnels when trying to Rift to Gracklstugh... It's always... been... a trap!</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">Demogorgon Summoned. </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">Sig, still under the effects of Madness that made him forget the existence of everyone else, was bound in Shuushar's net in his sleep. Meanwhile Shuushar transformed -- his head splitting apart in two and tentacles sprouting all over! Shuushar managed to summon his master Demogorgon using the cultist ritual circle while the Party rested in the cavern.</span></span></li><li><span id=\"docs-internal-guid-6f77410a-7fff-9d2b-91c1-5082d86a8b62\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">Next Time. </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: transparent; font-size: 11pt; white-space-collapse: preserve; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;\">Demogorgon is currently breaking through the wall of the cavern, trying to get at the Party! Shuushar is attacking Sig and Kronk! The Party must now try to escape...</span></span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.7999999999999998;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br></p><font color=\"#ffffff\"><div><br></div></font></span></div><div><br></div><div><br></div>",
  "visibleTo": [
    "__ALL__"
  ],
  "group": "Session Summaries"
}